{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Take one jar.</b> I do not know what it was of — of silver or of gold or of earthenware. Scripture says צנצנת — something that peers out from its fellow: an earthenware vessel, for it is from earth, from which seeds peer out and grow from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The passage moves from uncertainty about the material to deriving from the word צנצנת itself that it was earthenware; rendered as it stands without smoothing the logical leap."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:17.320683141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}